1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:02,300
<i>When will we meet
your new supplier?</i>

2
00:00:02,433 --> 00:00:04,433
<i>Let the boss meet
the other boss.</i>

3
00:00:04,567 --> 00:00:06,600
<i> Hon, why are you still here?</i>

4
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:07,833
<i> I was just waiting for you.</i>

5
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:08,900
<i> How's mom?</i>

6
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:11,033
<i>Did you find someone
to watch over her?</i>

7
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:12,100
<i> Yes, I have.</i>

8
00:00:12,233 --> 00:00:13,133
<i> This is Clarissa.</i>

9
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:16,033
<i>She offered to be
your caregiver.</i>

10
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:17,900
<i>- Can you handle it?
- Oh, yes, Ma'am.</i>

11
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:19,567
<i>Who are you?
What are you doing here?</i>

12
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:20,733
<i> Hey, thief!</i>

13
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:22,000
<i> I just borrowed your helmet.</i>

14
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:24,000
<i>What's going on there?
Never mind.</i>

15
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:25,133
<i> Better come with us.</i>

16
00:00:25,267 --> 00:00:26,400
<i>Explain yourself to the police.</i>

17
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:27,533
<i> Brother!</i>

18
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:29,767
<i>I missed you! It's been so long!</i>

19
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,100
<i> You haven't changed, huh?</i>

20
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:32,433
<i> We're still the same...</i>

21
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:33,700
<i> Handsome as ever.</i>

22
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:34,700
<i> Handsome as ever.</i>

23
00:00:34,833 --> 00:00:36,933
<i> Wow! It's so beautiful.</i>

24
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:38,633
<i> Boss Idol!</i>

25
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:40,067
<i> You're also here.</i>

26
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,133
<i> How come you're alone?</i>

27
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:42,800
<i> Actually, he's not alone.</i>

28
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:44,300
<i> Let's eat, come and join us.</i>

29
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:45,267
<i> No, thanks.</i>

30
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,700
<i>Why did you really come home,
Brother?</i>

31
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:47,933
<i>I just want to forget something.</i>

32
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:49,300
<i> What? Oh, I get it...</i>

33
00:00:49,433 --> 00:00:50,300
<i> Who?</i>

34
00:00:50,433 --> 00:00:51,267
<i> You ask too many questions.</i>

35
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,567
<i> I worry about you.</i>

36
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,633
<i>- Come on, I can handle it.
- If you say so.</i>

37
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:56,233
<i> Why is he still here?</i>

38
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:57,467
<i>You don't know how to eat
with your hands?</i>

39
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,500
<i> I do, look.</i>

40
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:00,867
<i> You don't. Admit it!</i>

41
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,200
<i> It's like this.</i>

42
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:03,733
<i>You've got something
on your face.</i>

43
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:05,767
<i>- Did you enjoy?
- Your ex is really good.</i>

44
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,000
<i> Even if she's just pretending,</i>

45
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:09,967
<i> you're still affected.</i>

46
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,833
<i> Do you still love her?</i>

47
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:16,133
<i> [OBB]</i>

48
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:35,900
<i> [UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

49
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:47,300
Oh...

50
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:49,033
why are we stopping?

51
00:01:49,167 --> 00:01:51,633
Ma'am, I think we have
a flat tire.

52
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:52,800
Then what are you waiting for?

53
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:54,333
Go and check it!

54
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:58,567
[TENSE INQUISITIVE
MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:02:11,233 --> 00:02:13,467
Well? Hurry up!

56
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,133
You, get the spare.

57
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,767
Madam, the spare is broken.

58
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,567
I haven't had it fixed yet.

59
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,200
Idiots!

60
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:24,133
Fools!

61
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,233
Why are you quiet
all of a sudden?

62
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:28,800
What is it?

63
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,000
Do you still love her?

64
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,933
Well...

65
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,400
I'm still fond of her.

66
00:02:42,933 --> 00:02:45,833
Our break-up was
a mutual decision.

67
00:02:45,967 --> 00:02:48,233
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,100
And I feel like we still have
some bitterness about it.

69
00:02:56,033 --> 00:02:58,533
What happened in your
love story?

70
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:00,133
Tell me the story.

71
00:03:01,967 --> 00:03:03,733
Why are you...

72
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:06,533
so interested, Joey?

73
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:12,767
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,233
[SIGHS]

75
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,067
No frowning allowed.

76
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,867
The store will lose money.

77
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:22,600
I lost, Brother.

78
00:03:22,733 --> 00:03:24,800
My crush seems
to like someone else...

79
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:27,567
or maybe she just
doesn't like me.

80
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:29,633
She's ignoring me.

81
00:03:29,767 --> 00:03:32,167
Kids today...

82
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,800
one drawback and they give up.

83
00:03:34,933 --> 00:03:36,867
What was your message?
Let me see.

84
00:03:39,467 --> 00:03:40,500
“My crush...”

85
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:42,833
What's this? Are you serious?

86
00:03:42,967 --> 00:03:43,833
Okay, this.

87
00:03:43,967 --> 00:03:45,600
“Hi.”

88
00:03:45,733 --> 00:03:48,000
“Are you still awake?”

89
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:49,800
“Are you going to rest now?”

90
00:03:50,967 --> 00:03:52,767
No wonder.

91
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,300
That's so cliché.

92
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:56,233
That doesn't work anymore.

93
00:03:56,367 --> 00:03:57,700
How, then?

94
00:03:58,867 --> 00:04:03,167
You need presence of mind.

95
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:05,233
First, find out her interests.

96
00:04:05,367 --> 00:04:06,733
What does she like?

97
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,800
She likes action movies.

98
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:15,333
- Oh? For real?
- Yes, yes.

99
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,633
Like Joey.

100
00:04:18,767 --> 00:04:19,633
[SCOFFS]

101
00:04:19,767 --> 00:04:20,867
I'm not interested.

102
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,933
If you don't want to tell me,
fine.

103
00:04:24,067 --> 00:04:25,167
[CHUCKLES]

104
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:26,733
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:28,067
Okay, fine.

106
00:04:28,233 --> 00:04:29,667
You're so cranky.

107
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:35,700
So, at first...

108
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:41,400
Zoey and I were fine.

109
00:04:42,633 --> 00:04:46,367
We were just starting
our careers.

110
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:50,133
Both driven, very much happy.

111
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:55,367
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:04:57,933 --> 00:05:00,033
<i> Oh my gosh, they want me?</i>

113
00:05:01,433 --> 00:05:02,933
[GIGGLES]

114
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:10,200
<i> You're late again.</i>

115
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:13,100
<i>I'm sorry, something happened
in Fairview.</i>

116
00:05:13,233 --> 00:05:15,267
<i> I had to cover for it.</i>

117
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,267
<i> But here...</i>

118
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,867
<i> a peace offering.</i>

119
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,333
<i> Your favorite.</i>

120
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:22,767
<i> Thank you.</i>

121
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,400
[CHUCKLES]

122
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:26,833
<i> How's work?</i>

123
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,333
<i> Andrew...</i>

124
00:05:30,467 --> 00:05:33,967
<i>my chief offered me
a field agent position.</i>

125
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,333
<i>Perfect! That's what you wanted,
right?</i>

126
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:38,500
<i> In Valmora.</i>

127
00:05:38,633 --> 00:05:41,100
<i>Up north, they want me
to relocate.</i>

128
00:05:41,233 --> 00:05:42,233
<i> I haven't answered yet...</i>

129
00:05:42,367 --> 00:05:45,167
<i>because I want us
to talk about it.</i>

130
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,633
<i> Zoey, my work is here.</i>

131
00:05:48,567 --> 00:05:50,400
<i>My team is here.
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

132
00:05:50,533 --> 00:05:52,700
<i> I want to build a future here.</i>

133
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:55,333
<i> And besides, my mom is here.</i>

134
00:05:55,467 --> 00:05:57,267
<i>You know that?
She's sick.</i>

135
00:05:58,067 --> 00:06:00,033
<i>But it's up to you,
I can't stop you, right?</i>

136
00:06:00,167 --> 00:06:01,467
<i> Why would I?</i>

137
00:06:01,733 --> 00:06:03,467
<i> Do you want to accept the job?</i>

138
00:06:06,367 --> 00:06:08,267
<i> You know what?</i>

139
00:06:08,433 --> 00:06:11,800
<i>Maybe they will give me
other opportunities.</i>

140
00:06:11,933 --> 00:06:13,767
<i> I will just decline the offer.</i>

141
00:06:14,933 --> 00:06:17,267
<i>I don't want us to be apart,
Andrew.</i>

142
00:06:19,233 --> 00:06:20,633
<i> Just promise me...</i>

143
00:06:20,767 --> 00:06:23,900
<i> that even if we're both busy,</i>

144
00:06:24,167 --> 00:06:26,200
<i>we will still make time
for each other.</i>

145
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:29,667
<i> That's what matters to me.</i>

146
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,467
<i> Okay.</i>

147
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,100
<i> I promise.</i>

148
00:06:33,233 --> 00:06:34,867
<i> That's a promise, okay?</i>

149
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,633
Looks like you guys
are doing fine after all.

150
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,900
What a waste of a love story.

151
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:44,467
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:47,700
I guess I'm partly to blame.

153
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,367
I made a promise to her, but...

154
00:06:52,967 --> 00:06:54,367
I didn't keep it.

155
00:06:55,667 --> 00:06:58,433
She got tired of waiting,
I guess.

156
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:04,367
<i> You're leaving, Zoey?</i>

157
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,367
<i> Isn't it obvious, Andrew?</i>

158
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:09,933
<i> I'm taking the job in Valmora.</i>

159
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:13,167
<i> Why?</i>

160
00:07:14,533 --> 00:07:18,233
<i>Andrew, I'm tired
of waiting for you.</i>

161
00:07:18,367 --> 00:07:21,333
<i>Sorry, I needed to do something.</i>

162
00:07:21,467 --> 00:07:24,533
<i>Oh, I didn't mean today
or last week.</i>

163
00:07:24,667 --> 00:07:26,600
<i>I look like a fool waiting
for you,</i>

164
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:29,233
<i>hoping that you'll give me time.</i>

165
00:07:29,367 --> 00:07:32,300
<i>But since you became famous,
you abandoned me.</i>

166
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:34,833
<i> I'm always alone.</i>

167
00:07:34,967 --> 00:07:36,967
<i> I didn't accept Valmora</i>

168
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:39,700
<i>because I wanted to be with you,</i>

169
00:07:39,833 --> 00:07:41,667
<i> to support you.</i>

170
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:46,800
<i>But it's been a while
since I prioritized myself.</i>

171
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:50,033
<i>Okay, what do you want me to do?</i>

172
00:07:50,167 --> 00:07:52,200
<i> I can leave that job.</i>

173
00:07:52,333 --> 00:07:54,167
<i>Please, I'll do anything,
just don't leave me, Zoey.</i>

174
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,933
<i>- Please.
- Don't you get it, Andrew?</i>

175
00:07:56,067 --> 00:07:57,900
<i> It's too late.</i>

176
00:07:58,033 --> 00:08:00,900
<i>I'm tired,
I want to be happy.</i>

177
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:06,800
<i> My ride's here.</i>

178
00:08:06,933 --> 00:08:11,000
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

179
00:08:15,833 --> 00:08:18,500
<i>Now you'll have all the time
for your work.</i>

180
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:21,833
<i> You have all the time.</i>

181
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,567
<i> Have fun, Andrew.</i>

182
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:29,900
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

183
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,533
<i> No wonder your ex is bitter.</i>

184
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:47,333
What happened after?

185
00:08:47,467 --> 00:08:49,100
You didn't chase after her?

186
00:08:49,233 --> 00:08:52,067
Well, we reconnect sometimes.

187
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,767
Social media.

188
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,167
Greetings.

189
00:08:55,333 --> 00:08:57,867
Christmas, New Year.

190
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,733
But that's all.

191
00:08:59,867 --> 00:09:01,233
Really?

192
00:09:02,233 --> 00:09:03,367
Yes.

193
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:08,133
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

194
00:09:08,267 --> 00:09:10,767
You still haven't answered
my question.

195
00:09:14,067 --> 00:09:15,733
Do you still love her?

196
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:22,567
[STIRRING ROMANTIC
MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:24,800
If I say yes,

198
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:27,667
will you be jealous?

199
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:30,867
[STIRRING ROMANTIC
MUSIC PLAYING]

200
00:09:31,867 --> 00:09:34,400
She likes action movies too,

201
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:36,600
so she knows how to fight.

202
00:09:36,733 --> 00:09:39,033
Her father taught her to.

203
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:41,733
That's why she knows taekwondo.

204
00:09:41,867 --> 00:09:43,433
She's also good
at hand-to-hand combat.

205
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:46,167
- She even taught me...
- Brother!

206
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,267
Where's the tip?

207
00:09:49,033 --> 00:09:51,300
Oh, anyway, she likes action
movies.

208
00:09:51,433 --> 00:09:53,633
Focus on that.
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

209
00:09:53,767 --> 00:09:55,133
What's her name?

210
00:09:55,267 --> 00:09:57,733
Never mind, you ask
too many questions.

211
00:09:57,867 --> 00:09:59,067
Okay, fine.

212
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,100
Okay, here...

213
00:10:00,233 --> 00:10:01,367
here's what you need to do.

214
00:10:01,533 --> 00:10:03,100
Tell her...

215
00:10:03,233 --> 00:10:04,167
“Hi, Crush.

216
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,800
There's a new action movie

217
00:10:05,933 --> 00:10:09,767
with Jillian Ward
and Raheel Bhyria.”

218
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:12,133
She'll say,
“OMG, I want to watch!”

219
00:10:12,267 --> 00:10:13,133
That's what she'll say.

220
00:10:13,267 --> 00:10:14,900
Then you say...

221
00:10:15,033 --> 00:10:19,367
“It's more exciting
with company.

222
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:24,300
Look, I have two tickets.
Want to watch?”

223
00:10:24,433 --> 00:10:25,667
That's what you say!

224
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,300
- Nice!
- Got it?

225
00:10:27,433 --> 00:10:29,700
Update me on what happens.

226
00:10:29,833 --> 00:10:31,433
Hundred percent success rate.

227
00:10:31,567 --> 00:10:33,933
Thanks, Brother.

228
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,600
[CHUCKLES]
Why would I be jealous?

229
00:10:36,733 --> 00:10:38,600
You're not really my boyfriend.

230
00:10:38,733 --> 00:10:41,700
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:43,633
You're really so cranky.

232
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:48,167
Okay, to answer your question...

233
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,900
past is past.

234
00:10:50,867 --> 00:10:52,667
I've moved on.

235
00:10:53,767 --> 00:10:55,900
Actually, I already...

236
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:59,467
love someone else.

237
00:11:00,867 --> 00:11:02,267
Who?

238
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:06,633
[HEART POUNDING]

239
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:07,933
I would like to buy...

240
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,267
Wait a second.

241
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:14,667
What do you want?

242
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:15,900
Four shampoos.

243
00:11:16,033 --> 00:11:17,767
Okay.

244
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:23,833
Oh, wait a minute.

245
00:11:23,967 --> 00:11:28,133
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:11:32,367 --> 00:11:34,500
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:11:34,633 --> 00:11:38,267
You know, they say
<i> Palawan</i> is beautiful...

248
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:41,167
You can swim, chill.

249
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:43,333
But it's even better...

250
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,700
when you have company.

251
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:46,967
Do you want to go...

252
00:11:47,233 --> 00:11:49,233
with me?

253
00:11:49,367 --> 00:11:50,833
Idiot!

254
00:11:50,967 --> 00:11:52,300
My change!

255
00:11:52,433 --> 00:11:53,667
Here you go.

256
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:57,867
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

257
00:12:04,433 --> 00:12:07,767
Are you serious? You're even
flirting with our customer?

258
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:10,000
I was just testing it.

259
00:12:10,133 --> 00:12:12,633
But it seems effective.

260
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:15,367
Hey, what are you laughing at?

261
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:17,867
Brother's teaching me
how to flirt.

262
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,033
[LAUGHS]
You, Peter?

263
00:12:20,167 --> 00:12:22,133
Teaching him?
[LAUGHS]

264
00:12:22,267 --> 00:12:24,867
You can't even bring home
a girl yourself.

265
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,567
[BENG CHUCKLES]
Auntie!

266
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,633
You know, if I were you two,

267
00:12:28,767 --> 00:12:30,733
I'd just focus on selling

268
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:32,800
because you have a better
chance of earning

269
00:12:32,933 --> 00:12:34,600
than getting girlfriends.

270
00:12:35,667 --> 00:12:37,100
Oh, these kids.

271
00:12:37,233 --> 00:12:38,700
[SIGHS]

272
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,500
Auntie Bebeng!
[SCREAMS]

273
00:12:45,633 --> 00:12:47,633
Both of you, get inside!

274
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,233
You monsters! Inside!

275
00:12:49,367 --> 00:12:50,500
Get in!

276
00:12:52,767 --> 00:12:55,833
You know, I don't believe you
don't have a boyfriend.

277
00:12:57,667 --> 00:12:58,767
I don't.

278
00:12:58,900 --> 00:12:59,700
None.

279
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:01,133
I don't.

280
00:13:03,767 --> 00:13:05,400
That's impossible.

281
00:13:07,133 --> 00:13:08,467
Why?

282
00:13:09,667 --> 00:13:11,767
Because I'm pretty?

283
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:13,667
I already know that.

284
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,233
[CHUCKLES]

285
00:13:15,367 --> 00:13:16,733
But, seriously.

286
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,733
You know what...

287
00:13:18,867 --> 00:13:20,733
this is the first time
I've dated again.

288
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,600
Even though my ex and I broke up
a long time ago,

289
00:13:24,733 --> 00:13:26,867
it's hard to recover.
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:32,000
Is that why you're here
in Valmora to forget?

291
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,900
That's the plan.

292
00:13:36,767 --> 00:13:38,933
But it feels like
I can't escape it.

293
00:13:40,567 --> 00:13:44,600
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:13:45,567 --> 00:13:47,400
Just to be clear...

295
00:13:47,533 --> 00:13:50,700
is this date of ours
just a game?

296
00:13:55,333 --> 00:13:56,667
Maybe.

297
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:00,967
You know, my friends say...

298
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:03,500
there's a lot of fishes
in the ocean.

299
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,033
Who knows?

300
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:09,433
I might catch the big fish here.

301
00:14:11,633 --> 00:14:12,800
[CHUCKLES]

302
00:14:12,933 --> 00:14:14,633
You know what, wait.

303
00:14:14,767 --> 00:14:17,667
We always talk about me.

304
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:20,167
You've dug up my whole past!

305
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:21,567
Now it's your turn.

306
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:24,100
How long have you been here?

307
00:14:25,067 --> 00:14:27,067
A long time.

308
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,300
And I fell in love
with the place.

309
00:14:29,467 --> 00:14:32,967
That's why I built this hotel,

310
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:36,167
and of course,
I decided to live here too.

311
00:14:37,333 --> 00:14:42,133
[PHONE RINGING]

312
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,133
If you'll excuse me,

313
00:14:44,267 --> 00:14:45,167
my boss is calling.

314
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,100
Yes, yes, go.

315
00:14:50,433 --> 00:14:54,633
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:14:57,233 --> 00:15:01,000
Well, my work...

317
00:15:01,633 --> 00:15:03,333
family...

318
00:15:03,467 --> 00:15:04,633
friends.

319
00:15:04,767 --> 00:15:06,267
Right?

320
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:08,033
Just like you.

321
00:15:09,067 --> 00:15:11,033
You love me already?

322
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:14,667
You're starting
to take this seriously.

323
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:17,400
Aren't we just pretending?

324
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:23,133
There are some things
that you cannot pretend, Joey.

325
00:15:24,167 --> 00:15:27,167
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:29,367
Anyway...

327
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:31,533
I just need to go
to the restroom.

328
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:36,567
[GRUNTS]

329
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:40,700
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

330
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:56,467
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

331
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:17,267
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

332
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:21,533
Thank you, Francis.

333
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,667
And I'm confirming
that Berdugo is on his way.

334
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,667
<i> He'll arrive early morning.</i>

335
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,367
Okay, everything is ready.

336
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,833
Good, good, good.
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

337
00:16:31,967 --> 00:16:35,600
Make sure you pick me up
right away.

338
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:36,600
- That's all.
- Yes, Madam.

339
00:16:36,733 --> 00:16:39,600
I'll send a car.

340
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:47,267
Andrew!

341
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:50,033
Joey...

342
00:16:53,567 --> 00:16:55,700
I just want to admit...

343
00:16:57,767 --> 00:17:00,333
that I'm jealous
because I like you.

344
00:17:00,467 --> 00:17:02,333
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:17:02,467 --> 00:17:03,800
You like me?

346
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:08,300
Wait, are you sure?

347
00:17:08,533 --> 00:17:10,767
I've felt this
for a long time, Andrew.

348
00:17:13,067 --> 00:17:16,467
I can't believe it, Joey.

349
00:17:19,467 --> 00:17:22,667
But what about Peter?

350
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:24,733
Isn't he...

351
00:17:24,867 --> 00:17:26,133
Peter?

352
00:17:26,267 --> 00:17:28,833
Don't mind him,
he's just my best friend.

353
00:17:28,967 --> 00:17:30,200
I already friend-zoned him.

354
00:17:30,333 --> 00:17:33,933
I never felt anything for him.

355
00:17:34,067 --> 00:17:35,967
Nothing at all!

356
00:17:37,033 --> 00:17:38,933
This feeling I have

357
00:17:39,067 --> 00:17:40,967
is only for you, Andrew.

358
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:45,167
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC CONTINUES]

359
00:17:53,133 --> 00:17:54,467
I knew it!

360
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,100
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

361
00:17:56,233 --> 00:17:58,033
I can't believe you, Joey!

362
00:17:58,167 --> 00:18:00,033
That really hurts!

363
00:18:00,167 --> 00:18:02,267
It hurts so much.

364
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,967
I'm sorry, Peter.

365
00:18:04,967 --> 00:18:07,367
But I never liked you.

366
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,233
Just please accept it.

367
00:18:13,367 --> 00:18:15,067
Maybe you could give me
a chance.

368
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,600
Who knows...

369
00:18:16,733 --> 00:18:19,367
Who knows,
maybe you'll love me too.

370
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:23,000
I'm sorry, Peter, but Andrew
and I love each other.

371
00:18:26,167 --> 00:18:27,933
Come on, Joey.

372
00:18:31,267 --> 00:18:33,133
Joey, wait.

373
00:18:33,267 --> 00:18:34,700
Joey...

374
00:18:35,733 --> 00:18:37,167
<i> Joey!</i>

375
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:39,367
Joey...

376
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,533
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

377
00:18:40,667 --> 00:18:42,200
Joey...

378
00:18:43,233 --> 00:18:44,767
Joey.

379
00:18:45,567 --> 00:18:47,233
Brother, wake up.

380
00:18:47,367 --> 00:18:48,767
Joey...

381
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,067
Brother, wake up.

382
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,167
Peter, wake up!

383
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,933
What?

384
00:18:54,067 --> 00:18:56,500
What's your problem?
I was sleeping!

385
00:18:56,667 --> 00:18:58,200
Peter, you were dreaming.

386
00:18:58,333 --> 00:18:59,367
It seemed bad.

387
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:01,067
Like a nightmare.

388
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:03,267
And you kept saying one name...

389
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:06,467
- What?
- Joey! Joey!

390
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:08,800
Is she the Joey
you told me about...

391
00:19:08,933 --> 00:19:10,300
the one who loves action movies?

392
00:19:11,967 --> 00:19:13,300
Wait...

393
00:19:14,433 --> 00:19:17,100
isn't Joey the girl you liked
in Manila?

394
00:19:17,333 --> 00:19:19,033
That's her, right?

395
00:19:19,167 --> 00:19:20,500
That's her!

396
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,633
Is she the reason you came back,
Brother?

397
00:19:25,567 --> 00:19:27,367
Is she the one you want
to forget?

398
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:31,333
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:19:37,533 --> 00:19:39,000
Zoey...

400
00:19:43,067 --> 00:19:44,933
Zoey, what are you doing here?

401
00:19:45,067 --> 00:19:46,600
Someone might see us.

402
00:19:46,733 --> 00:19:48,767
I just want to know something.

403
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:52,400
Are you really with Joey?

404
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:59,267
I think you're drunk.
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,767
I'll take you back
to your date, okay? Come on.

406
00:20:01,933 --> 00:20:05,000
Don't change the subject,
Andrew.

407
00:20:05,133 --> 00:20:06,733
Tell me.

408
00:20:07,533 --> 00:20:09,633
Are you with Joey?

409
00:20:23,233 --> 00:20:27,167
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:20:29,833 --> 00:20:32,633
<i>Will you be getting the couple
bracelet, Ma'am?</i>

411
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:35,833
<i> Yes.</i>

412
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,233
<i> Oh, it's a couple bracelet.</i>

413
00:20:37,367 --> 00:20:40,133
<i>I thought it was just
a friendship bracelet.</i>

414
00:20:44,233 --> 00:20:46,067
[SIGHS]

415
00:20:51,533 --> 00:20:53,367
The two are gone.

416
00:20:55,033 --> 00:20:57,400
<i> Where's Andrew?</i>

417
00:20:57,533 --> 00:21:01,500
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

418
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,333
Answer the question, Andrew.

419
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:22,267
Wait, why are you asking?

420
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:25,000
Because I feel like
you're doing it on purpose!

421
00:21:25,133 --> 00:21:28,100
You're too close to Joey!

422
00:21:28,233 --> 00:21:31,600
And I know you're trying
to do that to make me jealous!

423
00:21:31,733 --> 00:21:33,100
Wait, wait.

424
00:21:33,867 --> 00:21:36,367
We're just pretending, okay?
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

425
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,500
And besides...

426
00:21:38,633 --> 00:21:40,900
Why are you jealous of Joey?

427
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,767
We're not together
anymore, right?

428
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:45,533
I know.

429
00:21:46,533 --> 00:21:48,200
It's my fault.

430
00:21:49,533 --> 00:21:51,300
I left, I walked away,

431
00:21:51,433 --> 00:21:53,633
and I regret that.

432
00:21:55,433 --> 00:21:58,033
That's why I want you back,
Andrew.

433
00:22:01,933 --> 00:22:05,967
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

434
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:26,533
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

435
00:22:32,067 --> 00:22:36,367
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

436
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,867
Hey, what are you peeking at?

437
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,533
- Come on, take the shot!
- I just want to know

438
00:22:41,667 --> 00:22:42,733
whose car this is.

439
00:22:42,867 --> 00:22:44,600
You and Andrew aren't really
together, right?

440
00:22:44,733 --> 00:22:46,967
Or are you starting to have
feelings for him?

441
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:50,333
Didn't you say you own
this resort?

442
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:51,667
What do you do for your boss?

443
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:54,000
What if we treat you to dinner?

444
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:55,133
I have to decline.

445
00:22:55,267 --> 00:22:57,700
I have a very important meeting
tomorrow night.

446
00:22:57,833 --> 00:23:00,233
And this meeting
is to expand my business.

447
00:23:00,367 --> 00:23:01,600
I'll just go back to my room.

448
00:23:01,733 --> 00:23:02,767
What are you doing?

449
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:05,967
What if we ambush Delilah
tomorrow?

450
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:08,333
Boss, I found the people
looking for you.
